CDialogTree
{
Name=The Crypt's Dead
Portrait=!None
Should Have Voiceovers=0
Default Canceled Node Action=
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 retreat
Text=Bones in a broken coffin, and the smell of old dust.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 retreat read
Text=<You crouch over the bones.> This one died twice. The wound that killed him is two hundred years old and the marks over it are a month at most: something dug him up, used him, and lost him again. He was a Templar, and the second time he fought he was fighting for the other side.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 plateau
Text=A coffin lid lies broken beside a hollow of grave dust.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 plateau read
Text=<The dust remembers better than the bone does.> The same man has been killed nine times in this spot. There is not enough of him left to rise a tenth, and the part of him that should have gone somewhere two hundred years ago is still here, wound through the rock like a root. Whatever holds this place does not distinguish between its garrison and its enemies.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 ante
Text=A coffin, opened from the inside.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 ante read
Text=<From the inside, and recently.> This one was not raised by the necromancer who took this crypt. The mark on it is older than his work and cruder, and it does not belong to either army down here. Somebody was practising in these corridors long before the siege, and nobody in this place has mentioned it.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 burial
Text=An undisturbed coffin, older than the battle that came through here.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 burial read
Text=<You leave the lid where it is.> The ones this crypt was built for are still in it, and they are quiet in the way the dead are supposed to be. Whatever the wish did, it took the garrison and the horde and left the original tenants alone. You could take that as mercy. A colder reading is that a wish only binds what it was asked about, and these were not asked about.
Should Have Voiceover=0
}
